  ) +
  geom_line(
    data = normal_overlay, aes(x, y), color = "firebrick", linewidth = 0.8
  ) +
  facet_wrap(~predation_depth, scales = "free") +
  labs(x = "Trophic length", y = "Density")









We see that the ‘predation depth’ cleanly separates our three modes of the trophic level distribution. So we will go for an ordinal model the classify these modes and model each of the mode individually as a gaussian.
To discuss: does each category look Gaussian enough on its own (histogram + overlay, QQ plot, Shapiro test), are the variances comparable across categories or does the model need category-specific dispersion, and how this connects back to the ordinal-vs-continuous modeling choice raised earlier.

